      "probability": 0.72,
      "rationale": "The observed spread (range 1.6316–1.6959, SD ≈ 0.0092) is small relative to the mean and shows no systematic trend across days 1–10. The distribution appears roughly symmetric around 1.6689 with no clustering by day or event number. This is consistent with random measurement error in a well-maintained pendulum rig. No intervention needed; baseline is stable and reproducible. Continue post-baseline campaign to establish instrumental drift rate.",
