      "evidenceAgainst": []
    },
    {
      "label": "Uncontrolled thermal drift (small but present) masquerading as noise",
      "probability": 0.15,
      "rationale": "Day 8 (events 166–175) shows slightly elevated variance and lower minimum values (1.6316, 1.6338) compared to other days. If ambient temperature drifted during day 8 without returning, pendulum length would shift, lengthening period. However, days 9–10 show no sustained shift toward longer or shorter periods, and the baseline mean itself is stable. This weakly supports thermal drift as a *transient* effect (not ongoing). Requires: thermometer co-logged with every trial starting day 11; reanalysis of day 8 thermal records if available.",
      "evidenceFor": [166, 167, 168, 169, 170, 171, 172, 173, 174, 175],
      "evidenceAgainst": [183, 184, 185, 186, 187, 188, 194, 195, 196, 197, 198, 199]
    },
    {
      "label": "Systematic operator error or calibration drift in beat-counting method",
      "probability": 0.10,
      "rationale": "If the operator's timing or beat-definition has drifted over 10 days (e.g., finger-tapping start/stop, clock reset), we would expect drift in mean, not just noise. Mean is stable at 1.6689; no evidence of an operator trend. Low prior on this because meticulous protocol is standard in this lab. Rule out only if post-baseline shows similar scatter under identical conditions.",
      "evidenceFor": [],
      "evidenceAgainst": [150, 151, 152, 166, 167, 168, 169, 170, 171, 172, 173, 174, 175, 183, 184, 185, 186, 187, 188, 194, 195, 196, 197, 198, 199]
    }
  ],
  "residual": 0.03,
  "summaryOfChange": "Established first baseline (n=96, mean 1.6689 ± 0.0092 beats) with no evidence of drift or systematic bias. The primary open question is whether observed scatter (SD ~0.92%) is purely instrumental or includes a small, transient environmental effect (thermal). Baseline is sufficiently stable to move to post-baseline phase; co-log temperature starting day 11 to discriminate thermal hypothesis. No exotic mechanism is warranted. Residual 3% reserved for possibility of unlogged experimental event on day 8 not yet reported."
}
